{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כנעוריה", :translit "ke-ne'ureha", :gloss "like her youth"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling with extra vav signals that girlhood-to-adulthood transition is only six months"}], :frame {:text "The plene spelling of נעוריה with an extra vav indicates the brevity of the transition period between girlhood (na'arah) and full adulthood (bogeret), which is only six months. The Mishnah describes that a girl is a na'arah for six months before becoming a bogeret (Niddah 5:7), a halakhic framework codified by Maimonides in his Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Ishut 2:1.", :sources ["Niddah 5:7" "Mishneh Torah, Hilkhot Ishut 2:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Plene spelling with extra vav signals that girlhood-to-adulthood transition is only six months", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:51.898336535Z", :model "glm-5.2"}